WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.378
Book Four, Proposition Three.

2
00:00:02.378 --> 00:00:07.914
About a given circle to circumscribe a triangle equiangular with a given triangle.

3
00:00:07.914 --> 00:00:18.850
Let A B C be the given circle, and D E F the given triangle; it is required to circumscribe about the circle A B C a triangle equiangular with the triangle D E F.

4
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.246
Produce E F in both directions to the points G and H.

5
00:00:23.246 --> 00:00:30.222
Find the center K of the circle A B C by Three One, and draw the radius K B across at random.

6
00:00:30.222 --> 00:00:42.149
On K B at the point K, construct the angle B K A equal to the exterior angle D E G, and the angle B K C equal to the exterior angle D F H, by One Twenty-Three.

7
00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:51.000
Through the points A, B, and C, draw L A M, M B N, and N C L touching the circle A B C by the Porism to Three Sixteen.

8
00:00:51.420 --> 00:01:04.714
Because L M, M N, and N L touch the circle at A, B, and C, and K A, K B, and K C are radii to the points of contact, by Three Eighteen the angles at A, B, and C are right angles.

9
00:01:04.714 --> 00:01:20.696
In the quadrilateral A M B K, which divides into two triangles, the four interior angles equal four right angles; since angles K A M and K B M are right, the remaining angles A K B and A M B equal two right angles.

10
00:01:20.696 --> 00:01:34.661
Yet by One Thirteen, the adjacent angles D E G and D E F also equal two right angles, and angle A K B equals angle D E G; subtracting equals, the remaining angle A M B equals angle D E F.

11
00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.798
Similarly, angle L N B equals angle D F E.

12
00:01:37.798 --> 00:01:43.101
Therefore, by One Thirty-Two, the third angle M L N equals angle E D F.

13
00:01:43.101 --> 00:01:51.092
Thus the triangle L M N is equiangular with the triangle D E F and is circumscribed about the circle A B C.

14
00:01:51.092 --> 00:01:52.660
Which was to be done.

15
00:01:53.080 --> 00:02:09.482
Proposition Four Three is the projective dual of Four Two: instead of copying interior angles onto a tangent to locate chords, Euclid copies exterior supplementary angles at the center K so that the cyclic quadrilateral A M B K recovers the interior angles at the tangent intersections.

16
00:02:09.482 --> 00:02:19.460
As Heath notes, because each central angle at K is supplementary to an angle of triangle D E F, each is less than two right angles, guaranteeing that the three tangents meet.

17
00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:30.930
Peletier and Borelli observed that drawing all three pairs of parallel tangents produces eight triangles in all: two circumscribed about the circle, and six for which the circle is an escribed circle.

18
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:42.400
In the GEOMETOR G-Index, node G one hundred fifty-one synthesizes twelve direct prerequisites across fifty-nine ancestor nodes, uniting center finding, tangent perpendicularity, and angle-sum duality.

19
